WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.410
In this video, you microsegment a three-tier application. Access control lists on two subnets let each tier talk to the next one on a single port, and drop everything else.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:25.200
The VPC demo-3tier holds a web, an app, and a database subnet, one virtual machine each. The goal: web may reach app only on port 8080, app may reach the database only on port 5432, and nothing else crosses tiers.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.830
Start with the app tier. Open the action menu of demo-app and select Edit Config, then the Access Control List tab.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.290
Add the first rule.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.860
Choose Allow-related, so replies come back,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.480
and To-lport, for traffic arriving at the subnet's ports.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.270
With priority 1010, the match lets the web subnet in on TCP port 8080.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.140
Add a second rule, with the action Drop and the same direction,

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:09.270
with the lower priority 1000, for all other traffic from the web subnet.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.850
Select Save.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:19.800
Now the database tier. Edit demo-db the same way, and add two rules on its Access Control List tab.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:37.670
The first rule allows the app subnet on TCP port 5432, at priority 1010.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.120
The second drops everything else from the web and app subnets, at priority 1000.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.700
Select Save.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.810
Open the console of demo-web.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.280
Log in as sles, with the password that cloud-init set.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:09.550
Request the app tier on port 8080.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.530
The app answers. This is the one path the web tier is allowed.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:23.800
Now ping the app tier, and try the database directly.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.410
Both fail. Ping to the app tier is dropped, and the web tier can't reach the database at all.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.610
Then open the console of demo-app.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.020
Log in as sles, with the password that cloud-init set.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:49.290
Request the database on port 5432, then ping it.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:58.700
The database answers on port 5432, and the ping is dropped. Each tier reaches the next one on one port only.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:09.731
Each tier now reaches the next one on exactly one port, and the web tier can't touch the database. Next, you publish a virtual machine to the outside with a DNAT rule.
